        "original_id": "8ba3ee77-0a91-576e-8a2e-41fe1a4b4320",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cher, Brian Higgins, Stuart McLennen, Paul Barry, Steven Torch, Matthew Gray, Timothy Powell, Mark Taylor, Brian Rawling\n- Products: The Very Best of Cher, Believe, Gold\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n- Topics: song releases, compilation albums, songwriting, production\n\nFacts:\n- Cher recorded the song \"Believe.\"\n- On October 19, 1998, Warner Bros. released \"Believe\" as the lead single from Cher's twenty-second album, Believe.\n- Brian Higgins, Stuart McLennen, Paul Barry, Steven Torch, Matthew Gray, and Timothy Powell wrote \"Believe,\" and Mark Taylor and Brian Rawling produced it.\n- In a 2000 interview, Cher said that she also wrote part of \"Believe.\"\n- The album The Very Best of Cher includes Cher's popular songs \"If I Could Turn Back Time,\" \"Believe,\" \"Gypsies, Tramps and Thieves,\" and \"Take Me Home.\"\n- The album Gold was released two years after Cher's multi-platinum compilation album The Very Best of Cher.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "401a2fd5-def6-50a7-8594-22cdec699174",
        "text": "Page: The Very Best of Cher. Sentence: The album includes many of Cher's most popular songs, such as \"If I Could Turn Back Time\", \"Believe\", \"Gypsies, Tramps and Thieves\" and \"Take Me Home\".\nPage: Believe (Cher song). Sentence: \"Believe\" is a song recorded by American singer-actress Cher.\nPage: Believe (Cher song). Sentence: It is the title track from her twenty-second album of the same name (1998), and was released as the lead single from the album on October 19, 1998 by Warner Bros.\nPage: Believe (Cher song). Sentence: It was written by Brian Higgins, Stuart McLennen, Paul Barry, Steven Torch, Matthew Gray and Timothy Powell, although Cher claimed later in a 2000 interview that she also wrote part, and was produced by Mark Taylor and Brian Rawling.\nPage: Gold (Cher album). Sentence: The album was released only two years after the multi-platinum \"The Very Best of Cher\".",
